((date 2026-10-10) (slug shorts-phase-b-round1)
 (hypothesis
  "Shorts Phase B round 1 (plan total-return-and-shorts-phase-b-2026-10-05 decisions 6-10): does a book-faithful short-only Weinstein book make money by itself over 26 years? v0 = Phase A soTs (structural Nearest buy-stop, neutral_blocks_shorts, slow-grind gate off) with every merged short fix armed (#3131/#3133 ticket at breakdown_price and the $17 floor on the order price, #3145 tightened_can_ratchet, #3146 share-class gate for shorts, #3148 FINRA maintenance) on the rb1-26 accounting (split-dividend guard, shorts pay dividends, DTB3 - 10 bp cash). v1 = v0 + #3221 (short_cancel_on_non_bearish true, short_entry_order_max_rest_weeks 4). Pre-registered at 853514278 (#3220): an arm passes when A (26y return ex cash interest > 0, log and dollar readings) and B (>= 2 of 3 S&P close-high-to-low bear periods > 0, both readings) hold jointly in >= 2 of 3 valid salts.")
 (base_scenario
  "shorts-phase-b-2026-10-09: lane A v0 at 10f725ffe (the 904746e8c launch was stopped for V6 = 1 AIG/AIG-WS, fixed by #3227), lane B v1 at 27881ae05 with a byte-identical v0 s0 replay; warehouse /tmp/snap_top3000_pit_v12pit 9,236 entries; pit-v12 top-3000 lists md5 deca56c7 (union 9,222); 2000-01-01 -> 2026-06-25; salts 0/1/2 are intraday path seeds (identical trade sets per arm). V6 = 0 every cell; validator_diff -check V6 v1 vs v0 exit 0 every salt; interest reconstruction +0.05 % of cashinteresttotal (gate +-2 %).")
