 (notes
  "ROUND 1 FAILED, round-2 condition NOT MET (two independent results-analyst reads agree, the second blind): stop single-name shorts; bear protection goes to the index-hedge decision as its own question. The aggregates above include cash interest; the rule reads ex interest. A ex interest: v0 -0.925..-0.936 log / -73.0..-73.5 %, v1 -0.795..-0.801 / -65.7..-66.0 %. B: only 2008-09 positive (v0 +0.124, v1 +0.100); 2000-02 (-0.036 / -0.115) and 2022 (-0.096 / -0.073) negative on both readings. WHY (v0 s0, log): exposure timing -0.30 (an SPY short on the book's own exposure path loses too; Bearish weeks hold the V-rebounds), single names -0.49 beyond that, costs -0.14 (88 % of borrow from the 25 %/yr sub-$17 tier). The shorted breakdowns rose after the fill (fell in 36 % / 34 % at 8 weeks) and the skipped top-N candidate pool is a coin flip vs SPY at 20-250 days: no rule inside this pool makes the book positive. The loss is failed breakdowns (103 / 93 never-lowered stop exits, all losers, -$758k / -$713k). No book-rule entry cohort is positive in both arms; exits are bounded (perfect-hindsight exits on every winner leave +1.3 % / +4.5 % ex interest). v1 - v0 +0.131..+0.135 log, V6-gated, from fewer trades of the same negative expectancy, about half from one data-defect trade (HRC -$52.7k); v1 worse in 2000-02 and 2008-09. v1 flags = REJECT-as-default, keep as axes. #3131 PASS; #3145 stays pending (Trailing-state freezes, NKTR = #2982 basis mix); #3146 V6 = 0; #3148 call justified. DEFECTS: forced covers pre-empt the trigger-bar short stop fill and are labelled stop_loss (14 / 13 per cell); HRC 2005-12-19 raw-close splice; A-D breadth fixture leaves the Momentum Index stuck pre-2017; foreign-currency listings in the pit-v12 lists (HSBA, CELSIA, SBER); pack short-side readings (#3214). Writeup dev/experiments/shorts-phase-b-2026-10-09/results/results-2026-10-10.md; scripts results/analysis/run_all.sh."))
